casebook startup-demo v1
source "quorum fixture: start-up bypass and on-delays" dated 2026-10-27 by "quorum project"
note "Suction pressure dips while a pump starts, so low suction in the first 30 s of a start is expected and must not"
note "raise a cavitation alarm. A guard door switch must read open for 2 s before it stops the machine, so a bounce"
note "does not. Flow that stays low for 10 s is a fault. A guard opened in the last minute is still worth an alarm."

observe motor_started "the motor start command is on"
observe suction_low   "suction pressure below the limit"
observe door_open     "the guard door switch reads open"
observe flow_low      "discharge flow below the limit"

reading starting      "the first 30 s after a start" when motor_started within first 30s
reading door_off      "the guard door switch has read open for 2 s" when door_open for 2s
reading no_flow       "flow has stayed low for 10 s" when flow_low for 10s
reading door_recently "the guard was open at some point in the last minute" when door_off within last 1m

claim cavitation   "low suction while running" severity 6 needs suction_low
claim flow_fault   "no flow" severity 5 needs no_flow
claim guard_open   "the guard is open" severity 9 needs door_off
claim guard_was    "the guard was open recently" severity 2 needs door_recently

excuse start_transient "suction dips while the pump starts" needs starting
start_transient undercuts cavitation

action run idle
action alarm when any cavitation flow_fault guard_was
action stop safe when any guard_open
prefer stop over alarm over run
